a 250-buy/148-sell storm in run #38), avoidable error rate 4.3% (the dashboard's
27.3% was pre-fix).

THE REAL LEAK, found by drilling run-#52 events: **overburden → strand → die.**
`carry` is *weight* not slots (16 items = 20/21). A near-full char that grabs one
heavy meat/ore crosses used>cap; the server's overburden penalty cripples its
movement so the stamina-gated walk home is unaffordable, and nothing sheds the
weight — 1681 `overburdened` events across 19 chars, one stuck 939 ticks, burning
a scarce world slot until poison kills it. Only 74 of 687 pickups ever `returned`
to be sold. That is why gold is pinned at ~14 despite healthy looting.

Shipped **explorer/0.15.0** (git 62152eb): (1) pursue/grab loot only when not full
so chars stop crossing into overburden; (2) when used>=cap, `drop` the least-useful
carried item (clutter→ore, never KEEP/gear) above the full-retreat, so a stranded
char sheds weight and walks its remaining loot home. All 3 new assertions
mutation-checked; suite 200 passed/2 skipped; reaper container gate green; 400-frame
replay clean on 0.15.0.

