neighbour make-up across 42 stuck deaths = walkable 100 / SOLID 8 / occupied 28 / unknown 32.
=> TERRAIN-CORNERING REFUTED (only 8/168 solid). Buckets: had_exit_didnt_move 35, fleeing 9,
cornered_unseen 6, out_of_stamina 1. Then the DECISIVE actions cross-check (actions_sent +
action_errors, last 15 ticks/death): 36/51 dying chars ISSUED >=1 MOVE (129 moves total; +13
attack, +2 use); the other 15 issued NOTHING (idle). action_errors: not_enough_stamina 24,
no_such_item 14, out_of_range 7, unknown_character 7. => the failure is MOVES NOT LANDING, not a
missing decision-to-move and not terrain. Two sub-mechanisms: (A) ~71% issue moves but stay put
— stamina-REJECTED (not_enough_stamina) and/or tile-BOUNCES (moved toward a blocked/occluded
tile despite a walkable option); (B) ~29% idle (rest/craft while a predator closes).
REVISED 0.37 DESIGN BASIS: the anti-stuck lever is "make escape moves LAND" — primarily the
STAMINA ECONOMY (don't let a threatened char get stamina-stranded next to a predator; 0.34
urgent-moves bypass the 1.5x margin but not_enough_stamina still fires 24x, so either they aren't
triggering here or the char is below the raw ~20 cost), and secondarily escape-DIRECTION choice /
bounce-recovery (pick a KNOWN-walkable neighbour, and after a bounce try a different one). NOT a
dodge, NOT terrain-avoidance. This is subtler than iter37 framed it. Still gated on operator
greenlight (strategy change => full gate + redeploy).
NEXT PASS: refine the (A) split (stamina-stranded vs tile-bounce fractions) to size the lever;
health; wishlist. If greenlit, build 0.37 on this basis.
